%T A400729 0,0,2,1,1,0,0,2,1,2,0,0,1,1,0,0,3,0,0,6,4,2,2,0,0,2,1,3,0,1,1,2,0,0,
%U A400729 2,2,1,3,0,2,0,0,3,1,0,2,1,0,2,1,0,3,2
%N A400729 The sequence of y-values that occur when drawing a sequence of squares in the plane with integer side lengths such that the bottom-left corner of the k-th square is at the nonnegative integer point (k, a(k)) and the square has side length s_k, subject to the conditions that (1) every initial sequence has the property that the interior of each square has a distinct pattern made by the perimeters of the other squares, and (2) we greedily minimize the side length and then minimize the y-value.
%H A400729 Peter Kagey, <a href="https://codegolf.stackexchange.com/q/291882/53884">The Eternal Internal Patterns of Squares</a>, Code Golf Stack Exchange.
%e A400729 The first square has side length A400728(0)=1, and y-value a(0)=0; the next has side length A400728(1)=2 and y-value a(1)=0, and so on. The index of each square is marked in the lower right corner.
